{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"e6d4813f22ddb02ab4ff047e0d9770a56e42fd25"},"timestamp":1533489910,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzNDc3MTYwMTA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2745","origin":"github"},"title":"Hidden folders files not saved when using `datalad save`","message":"#### What is the problem?\nWhen using `datalad save` on a folder container a hidden-folder, the files from the hidden-folder are not saved. In my situation, I have user dependant files that are placed inside a hidden config folder which I want to save and publish to my remotes. However, currently, I must call an explicit save on that hidden folder for it to be successfully saved.\n#### What steps will reproduce the problem?\n1. Using any dataset, create a hidden folder `.name` inside a standard folder.\n2. `datalad save` the parent folder\n3. The hidden folder is not saved\n#### What version of DataLad are you using? On what operating system?\nDatalad: datalad 0.10.1\nOS: Ubuntu 18.04.1 LTS\n#### Is there anything else that would be useful to know in this context?\nWhen calling `datalad save` with the hidden folder path, it is successfully saved. Only when trying to save it through a save on a parent folder is the hidden folder content not saved.","files":null}]}